      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When high GI foods are consumed, the quick absorption of sugar into the bloodstream triggers an insulin response. In people with type 2 diabetes, their insulin-producing beta cells are already fatigue, making it harder for the body to manage spikes in blood sugar. Meanwhile, insulin's role is to help cells absorb glucose, but when glucose levels are high, excess glucose builds up in the bloodstream, as if the body needs \"withdrawal\". This excess glucose is then stored as glycogen or fat.",
